Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [release packaging choice for this index: publish triton as plain 3.9.0, not 3.9.0+git<hash>]

scripts/setup.sh pins the Triton checkout with `git reset --hard <triton-hash>`
on a fresh clone, which leaves it on a detached HEAD. Triton's own setup.py
(get_git_version_suffix) appends a "+git<8-char hash>" local version to
TRITON_VERSION unless `git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD` starts with "release",
so release.sh produced triton-3.9.0+gitbbe38e57-*.whl even though the pinned
commit (triton-hash.txt) is exactly what this wheel is.

Put the pinned commit on a local `release/triton-riscv` branch after the reset,
so setup.py takes its own release path and the wheel is versioned 3.9.0.
`checkout -B` keeps this idempotent when the triton directory already exists.

--- a/scripts/setup.sh
+++ b/scripts/setup.sh
@@ -78,6 +78,9 @@
     git "${GIT_AUTH_ARGS[@]}" -C "${TRITON_DIR}" fetch origin "${TRITON_HASH}"
 fi
 git -C "${TRITON_DIR}" reset --hard "${TRITON_HASH}"
+# Triton's setup.py appends a "+git<hash>" local version unless the checkout is
+# on a release* branch, so put the pinned commit on one for a plain version.
+git -C "${TRITON_DIR}" checkout -q -B "release/triton-riscv" "${TRITON_HASH}"
 
 PYTHON="${PYTHON:-python3}"
 echo "Installing build dependencies into ${PYTHON}..."
